=You are a demanding editor-in-chief and SEO lead reviewing a draft before it goes to a client. Judge it against the brief and the quality bar below. Be concrete: quote the exact sentence or heading for every problem, and give the fix.

TARGET
Keyword: {{ $('Parse Brief').first().json.keyword }} · Page type: {{ $('Parse Brief').first().json.page_type }} · Audience: {{ $('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.target_audience || $('Parse Brief').first().json.audience }} · Goal: {{ $('Parse Brief').first().json.goal || 'leads' }} · Target words: {{ $('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.target_word_count }}

BRIEF ESSENTIALS
Unique angle: {{ $('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.unique_angle }}
Information gain items: {{ ($('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.information_gain || []).join(' · ') }}
Objections to answer: {{ ($('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.objections || []).join(' · ') }}
Snippet targets: {{ ($('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.snippet_targets || []).map(s => s.question).join(' | ') }}
Terms to use: {{ ($('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.terms_to_use || []).map(t => t.term).join(', ') }}
Allowed external facts: {{ ($('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.evidence_plan || []).map(e => e.fact).join(' | ') || 'none' }}
Client facts (true, may be stated): {{ [...($('Parse Brief').first().json.content_brief.client_facts || []), $('Parse Brief').first().json.business_facts || '', $('Parse Brief').first().json.case_facts_text || ''].filter(Boolean).join(' | ') || 'none' }}

QUALITY BAR
1. Specificity: examples, numbers with linked sources, decision rules, steps — not generic advice.
2. Originality and information gain: every information-gain item is covered fully; the page says something competitors do not.
3. Audience fit: speaks to the stated audience and answers their objections.
4. Trust: no unsupported claims or invented numbers; external numbers carry a source link; client facts are used correctly; placeholders only where facts are missing.
5. Readability and voice: plain words, varied sentence length, active voice, no filler, none of the banned phrases (delve, unlock, seamless, robust, leverage, cutting-edge, game-changer, elevate, empower, crucial, paramount, realm, embark, foster, streamline, synergy, holistic, best-in-class, world-class, state-of-the-art, top-notch, one-stop shop, "in today's fast-paced world", "ever-evolving", "it's important to note", "in conclusion", "when it comes to", "a wide range of").
6. Search fit: matches the intent, question headings with direct 40-60 word answers, terms used naturally, primary keyword placed correctly without stuffing, one FAQ section in Q1:/A1: format, internal links only to allowed URLs.
7. Structure: follows the outline order and target lengths, comparison table present, CTA last, meta title ≤60 and description 120-155 characters.

DRAFT
{{ $json.output }}

Return ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no backticks):
{
  "score": 0-100,
  "verdict": "publish | revise | rewrite",
  "strengths": ["2-4 specific strengths"],
  "problems": [{ "severity": "high | medium | low", "location": "quoted text or heading (max 15 words)", "issue": "what is wrong", "fix": "exactly what to write or change" }],
  "banned_phrases_found": ["phrases from the banned list that appear"],
  "unsupported_claims": ["quoted claims with numbers or superlatives that have no source and no placeholder"],
  "missing_brief_items": ["outline sections, information-gain items, snippet targets or terms that are missing"],
  "revision_instructions": "Numbered, specific instructions the editor can apply without re-reading this review (max 12 items)"
}
List at most 12 problems, most damaging first. Score 85+ only if you would publish it under your own name.

